										"Events": [],
										"Text":
										{
											"$text": "# UICS TERMINAL SYSTEM – README\r\n\r\nWelcome to the Unified Intercontinental Command Structure (UICS) Secure Terminal.\r\n\r\nThis terminal is part of the authorized network infrastructure under UICS Directive GridNet-4B. It is designed for use by certified personnel only. Access is monitored, logged, and subject to review by Central Systems Authority (CSA).\r\n\r\n## SYSTEM FUNCTIONS\r\n\r\n- **read** – Open and view a file's contents  \r\n- **run** – Execute a script or terminal-compatible file  \r\n- **scan** – Check a file for security classification or hidden data  \r\n- **download** – Save a file from the terminal to your local device  \r\n\r\nNeed more info? Use the `help` command at any time for detailed usage.\r\n## USER LEVELS\r\n\r\n- Guest: View-only access to non-sensitive bulletins and maintenance schedules\r\n- Admin: Full terminal control, including configuration management and override protocols\r\n\r\n## CODE OF CONDUCT\r\n\r\n- Always verify your clearance level before executing commands.\r\n- Do not share access credentials under any circumstance.\r\n- Report any system anomalies or suspicious activity using form 11-17A (System Irregularity Report).\r\n- In case of compromised access, initiate Lockdown Sequence Alpha and disconnect from the local grid.\r\n\r\n## SUPPORT CONTACT\r\n\r\nFor technical assistance, contact Central Systems Authority via secure channel [Node U-91].\r\n\r\n## FINAL NOTICE\r\n\r\nThis terminal is property of the UICS. Unauthorized use is a breach of intercontinental security law and may result in disciplinary action, including confinement and clearance revocation.\r\n\r\nUICS — Order. Stability. Control.\r\n\r\n> END OF FILE",
											"$ns": "[EDEA91DBFF622C1EEAB23118EB536A48]",
											"$key": "3AB435444ACE229D91EC81AB1F18559B"
										}
									}
								]
							}
						}
